const faqs = [
  ['Who are the best spiral conveyor manufacturers?', 'The best spiral conveyor manufacturer depends on the load. Ryson and AmbaFlex are the specialists and cover cases, totes, and mass flow of bottles and cans. FlexLink and Dorner fit light products in a small footprint. Span Tech, Nercon, and Alliance Industrial build washdown or direct food contact spirals. Multi-Conveyor builds custom drum spirals for accumulation. These picks are based on each company\'s published specifications, not on testing.'],
  ['Who makes spiral conveyors?', 'Companies that publish a spiral conveyor product line include Alliance Industrial, AmbaFlex, Dorner, FlexLink, Multi-Conveyor, Nercon, Ryson International, and Span Tech. Ryson and AmbaFlex specialize in spirals. The others build spirals as one part of a wider conveyor range.'],
  ['Which spiral conveyor manufacturers handle a mass flow of bottles and cans?', 'Ryson publishes Mass Flow Spiral models for bulk bottles, cans, and jars, and AmbaFlex publishes the SpiralVeyor SVm for a mass flow of individual bottles and cans. Alliance Industrial also states that its spirals can move mass and bulk product. Most other spirals are built for single-file products, packs, or cases.'],
  ['How do spiral conveyor designs differ between manufacturers?', 'The main differences are where the drive sits and what the product rides on. Some spirals pull a slat chain from a single drive at one end. Others drive the chain from a sprocket on every tier, from a center drum, or from the belt edge. The conveying surface can be slats on a roller chain, plastic top chain, table-top chain, or modular plastic belt. These choices set the load rating, the washdown suitability, and the maintenance access.'],
  ['Which spiral conveyors are suitable for washdown?', 'Span Tech builds stainless steel spirals with washdown-capable modular plastic chain. Nercon publishes a washdown spiral rated for washdown pressure up to 1,500 psi. Alliance Industrial offers a sanitary side-drive spiral for direct food contact, and Ryson offers stainless steel versions of its case spirals. Confirm the cleaning method and chemicals with each supplier.'],
];
const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ "@type": "Question", "name": q, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": a } }))
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Best Spiral Conveyor Manufacturers: Top 8 Compared (2026)"
  description="The top 8 spiral conveyor manufacturers and what each is best for: cases, mass flow, small footprints, washdown. Compared on published specs, no paid placement."
  canonical={url}
  schema={[breadcrumbSchema, articleSchema, listSchema, faqSchema]}
>
<h1>Best Spiral Conveyor Manufacturers by Application</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">The best spiral conveyor manufacturer depends on the load. Ryson and AmbaFlex specialize in spirals and cover cases, totes, and mass flow. FlexLink and Dorner fit light products in tight spaces. Span Tech and Nercon build for washdown. This page compares the top 8 spiral conveyor manufacturers using each company's published specifications.</p>

<figure class="photo"><img src="/img/photos/spiral-ryson-slats.webp" width="1000" height="596" alt="Close view of overlapping dark slats curving around the central column of a stainless steel spiral conveyor." loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>The slat conveying surface on a Ryson spiral conveyor. <span class="photo-credit">Photo: <a href="https://ryson.com/spiral-conveyors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ryson</a></span></figcaption></figure>
<div class="usa-summary-box" role="region" aria-labelledby="criteria-heading">
<div class="usa-summary-box__body">
<h2 class="usa-summary-box__heading" id="criteria-heading">How this list was built</h2>
<div class="usa-summary-box__text">
<ul>
<li>A company is listed if it publishes a product page for a spiral conveyor that moves packaged goods, containers, or cases between elevations.</li>
<li>The list is alphabetical. We do not rank companies 1 to 8, because the best choice changes with the application.</li>
<li>"Best for" labels reflect each company's published specifications and product range.</li>
<li>Specifications are the manufacturer's own published figures, checked October 5, 2026. We have not tested any equipment.</li>
<li>No company paid to be listed. For how spirals work, see the <a href="/conveyor-types/spiral-conveyors/">spiral conveyor guide</a>.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>

