<table>
<thead>
<tr><th>If you need</th><th>Shortlist</th><th>Why</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Cases and totes with a published load rating</td><td>Ryson, AmbaFlex</td><td>Ryson rates case spirals to 1,800 lbs and High Capacity spirals to 3,600 lbs. AmbaFlex lists the SV for cartons, crates, and totes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mass flow of bottles and cans</td><td>Ryson, AmbaFlex</td><td>Both publish dedicated mass flow spirals.</td></tr>
<tr><td>The smallest footprint for light products</td><td>FlexLink, Dorner</td><td>FlexLink lists a 585 mm diameter. Dorner lists a 1,400 mm, four-tier helix.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Washdown or direct food contact</td><td>Span Tech, Nercon, Alliance Industrial</td><td>Stainless and washdown-rated designs, including a 1,500 psi rating from Nercon.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Accumulation time, not only elevation</td><td>Multi-Conveyor, AmbaFlex, Dorner</td><td>Each describes spirals used for buffering.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Non-standard geometry</td><td>Alliance Industrial, Multi-Conveyor</td><td>Both build spirals to order.</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

